# world/cocoaui.list — the conditional Cocoa GUI world layer
# (docs/cocoa_gui_design.md §12.3, sprint_cocoa_gui.md CG1). Loaded ONLY by
# the UI worker via `frontend::world::load_list(vm, path)` AFTER the base
# world is up — never from world/world.list, so the CLI, the WKWebView GUI,
# and the base test suite carry none of it.
#
# Same format as world.list: one .mst path per line, relative to THIS file's
# directory; blank lines and #-comments skipped. Files reserved 63+ (01-62 are
# taken by the base world; verify with `ls world/`).
63_cocoaui_stub.mst
# MacvmDelegate (the C6 delegate/action-target registry) loads BEFORE CocoaUI:
# CG4's `CocoaUI startup` references `MacvmDelegate actionTargetOn:` for the
# Workspace ⌘P/⌘D target, so the class must be declared when 64 compiles. The
# list order — not the filename number — is what fixes the forward reference.
65_cocoadelegate.mst
64_cocoaui.mst
# CocoaBrowser (CG7) loads after CocoaUI: startup resolves it BY NAME and asks
# it to register its view, so the file is optional — remove the line and the
# shell simply has no Browser entry.
66_cocoabrowser.mst
67_cocoafind.mst
# CocoaEditor (the class text editor tab) also self-registers by name:
# native NSTextView editing; Save recompiles live on the primary (uiDoit) +
# persists the diff to the image + world (host).
68_cocoaeditor.mst
# CocoaOutliner (the Strongtalk-style unfolding tree, LIVE ClassMirror
# reflection — the other half of the dual placement from CocoaBrowser's DB
# queries) also self-registers by name.
69_cocoaoutliner.mst
# CocoaCanvas (an RGBA drawing surface — pixel buffer + vector command batch,
# docs/CANVAS.md) also self-registers; needs 66 (CocoaBrowser hostService).
70_cocoacanvas.mst
# CocoaHelp (a read-only Markdown documentation tab, docs/macvm_help.md)
# also self-registers by name; no dependency on any other Cocoa GUI file.
71_cocoahelp.mst
# CocoaBrowser2 (V2, additive — V1's 66_cocoabrowser stays): a classic
# Smalltalk-80 category browser — system-category / class / protocol / method
# panes (categories from the M1 package lists, protocols derived heuristically
# from selectors) + a Comment/Definition/Source pane. Full affordances —
# browse AND write (accept method/class source, add/remove classes and
# methods, set comments) through the same host-service flows as V1;
# self-registers by name as the 'Browser V2' view.
72_cocoabrowser2.mst
# CocoaDebugger (DBG4, docs/gui_debugger_design.md): the native face of the VM
# HALT loop — a Debugger tab that shows the halted stack/source/frame, with
# Step Into/Over/Finish/Continue/Abort + a print-it field. Auto-fronts when the
# primary halts (breakpoint, `halt`, or Halt-on-Error). Self-registers by name.
73_cocoadebugger.mst
74_cocoascript.mst
# CocoaSpriteEditor (docs/asset_editors_design.md): the Sprite Editor window —
# Tools ▸ Sprite Editor…; edits GamePane hex-row sprites, saves sheet classes.
# The pure model (SpriteDoc) is a WORLD-list file so games and the headless
# battery can load it; this file is only the Cocoa face.
76_spriteed.mst
# CocoaSoundEditor (docs/asset_editors_design.md stage 6): Tools > Sound
# Editor — the ADSR instrument panel over prim 263's parametric synth wire.
77_sounded.mst
# CocoaMonitor (the Monitor tab): one table row per running VM (primary, UI
# worker, spawned workers) from the host's `monitorRows` roster verb, plus
# the UI BRIDGE band (`bridgeStatsLine` — the Cocoa side's own counters).
# Rides the ~4 Hz metrics beat at a user-selectable period; self-registers
# by name with the SF-Symbol magnifying glass.
86_coctests.mst
85_cocoamonitor.mst
# CocoaRealize (docs/appspec.md A2): the AppSpec framework's platform half —
# the only file in it that knows AppKit exists. Implements the realizer
# protocol from 89_apptoolwin.mst and installs itself as the realizer class,
# which is what makes declarative tools draw here. Loaded only by the UI
# worker, so headless images keep the null realizer.
92_cocoarealize.mst
# CocoaMixedStrip (docs/appspec.md A6): the Cocoa half of the Mixed Demo —
# the hand-built NSView its foreignView names, with an imperatively wired
# NSButton dispatching the same #bump the declarative one sends.
92a_appmixedstrip.mst
